    {
      "text": "小雨这才小声解释：“中国人说打折，跟你想的不一样。‘九折’是付百分之九十，只便宜百分之十。数字越小，才越便宜。”",
      "py": "Xiǎo yǔ zhè cái xiǎo shēng jiě shì: “Zhōng guó rén shuō dǎ zhé, gēn nǐ xiǎng de bù yí yàng. ‘jiǔ zhé’ shì fù bǎi fēn zhī jiǔ shí, zhǐ pián yi bǎi fēn zhī shí. shù zì yuè xiǎo, cái yuè pián yi.”",
      "en": "Only now does Xiaoyu explain quietly. \"Discounts in China don't work the way you think. A 'nine' discount means you pay ninety per cent—it's only ten per cent off. The smaller the number, the cheaper it is.\"",
